# Normalize line endings in the repository.
#
# The pre-commit hook `mixed-line-ending --fix=lf` rewrites every file to
# LF, but on Windows `core.autocrlf=true` converts them back to CRLF on
# checkout. The two fought each other: every commit failed with
# "Stashed changes conflicted with hook auto-fixes" and had to be
# retried. These attributes make the normalisation authoritative and
# platform-independent:
#
#   * text files are stored with LF in the repository and checked out
#     with the platform's native ending;
#   * binary files are never touched.
#
# `* text=auto eol=lf` is the safe default: it only affects files git
# already detects as text, and it makes the working tree LF everywhere so
# the pre-commit hook and the formatter agree with what is committed.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary artefacts — never line-ending converted.
*.safetensors binary
*.parquet binary
*.jsonl -diff
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp4 binary

# Generated reports and model cards: keep them diffable.
*.md text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
